    <string name="privacy_consent_title">Politique de confidentialité</string>
    <string name="privacy_consent_body">Reverb is a fully local podcast client. Before you start, here is how your data is handled.\n\nWe collect no personal information. There is no server, no account, no third-party SDKs, no analytics and no ads.\n\nYour data stays on this device. Subscriptions, history, favorites, downloads, listening time, stamps and settings are all stored in the app\'s private directory and removed on uninstall.\n\nWhat the network is used for.To search and play podcasts, your device directly contacts the publishers\' own RSS, audio and artwork URLs; when you tap "Import recommended feeds", it downloads a subscription list from this app\'s website. If your build offers show search, it also contacts public search APIs (Apple Podcasts, fyyd.de, gpodder.net). No credentials and no user identifiers are attached; see the full policy for the complete list.\n\nAbout the network-state permission. It is used to detect Wi‑Fi so that “download on Wi‑Fi only” works. In addition, the system playback and background-task libraries this app uses query the network type via a system API whose returned object may carry the Wi‑Fi network name (SSID). This app does not read, store or transmit that name.\n\nPermissions. Internet, network state, background audio playback, and notifications (requested only when you enable update reminders). No location, contacts, camera, microphone, SMS, call log or calendar access is requested.\n\nTapping “Agree and continue” means you have read and accept this policy.</string>
